{
  "name": "r9-chain-lost-carriage-record-restart-stays-held",
  "requires": "r9",
  "kind": "scenario",
  "side": "host",
  "log": "r9-vectors-membership-log",
  "note": "R9.3 (Astation r4 review 2): the first device-list write, the carriage record, fails and is lost entirely, so nothing about the carriage (here a conflicting window, C6_mac) reached the disk. Atem never evaluated it: it refuses the carriage unread, fences every remote principal in memory and halts. At restart the host is not frozen (it never learnt of a conflict) but held, since the fault was recorded (the fault record is a separate write that succeeded): no remote hello is admitted, not after a day and another orderly restart, and nothing re-carries the conflict. Only a managing device whose verified log ends at the host's head reconciles it.",
